    "title": "Mariners could replace $6.25 million free agent signing at MLB trade deadline - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Sullivan ,\n19 days ago The Seattle Mariners are 39-37, sitting atop the AL West, but their 1.5-game division lead isn't enough to feel comfortable with just yet. To solidify their status as postseason contenders, they need to continue winning games, and to do so, they might need some help at the MLB trade deadline. One of the top needs for this team is a player at a position who could replace a $6.25 million signing. Read full article",
